1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,782
This tutorial follows a maintenance ticket
in Oasis

2
00:00:02,782 --> 00:00:05,564
Crest Properties, from the Tenant's report
to closure,

3
00:00:05,564 --> 00:00:08,346
with the work assigned to the maintenance
supervisor.

4
00:00:08,346 --> 00:00:10,780
Signed in as the Tenant Ahmed Hassan,

5
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:13,215
open My Tickets and select Create Ticket.

6
00:00:13,215 --> 00:00:16,344
Give it a short title and describe the
problem.

7
00:00:16,344 --> 00:00:19,474
The property and unit come from the
Tenant's contract.

8
00:00:19,474 --> 00:00:23,647
Choose the category, HVAC, and the
priority, High, then select Create Ticket.

9
00:00:23,647 --> 00:00:26,081
The ticket joins the list as Open.

10
00:00:26,081 --> 00:00:28,516
Now sign in as the Company Admin.

11
00:00:28,516 --> 00:00:32,341
Khalid Rahman is on the staff list as the
Maintenance Supervisor,

12
00:00:32,341 --> 00:00:35,818
but tickets are assigned to people who can
sign in.

13
00:00:35,818 --> 00:00:38,600
In Settings, Users and staff, select New
User.

14
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,730
Enter his name and email, choose Company
User, the

15
00:00:41,730 --> 00:00:44,860
role for the maintenance team, and select
Provision User.

16
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:47,294
No password is set here: Khalid gets

17
00:00:47,294 --> 00:00:49,728
an email invite to choose his own.

18
00:00:49,728 --> 00:00:53,554
His login now appears in the Users list as
a Company

19
00:00:53,554 --> 00:00:57,031
User, with Resend invite in case the email
is lost.

20
00:00:57,031 --> 00:00:59,813
Now open the new ticket from Operations,
Tickets.

21
00:00:59,813 --> 00:01:02,247
Select Assign To and pick Khalid Rahman.

22
00:01:02,247 --> 00:01:04,682
The status moves to Assigned, and Khalid

23
00:01:04,682 --> 00:01:07,116
can update the tickets assigned to him.

24
00:01:07,116 --> 00:01:10,941
Reply to the Tenant with the visit time,
and set the

25
00:01:10,941 --> 00:01:14,419
estimated hours, so the Tenant knows when
to expect him.

26
00:01:14,419 --> 00:01:16,853
When the work starts, select Start Work.

27
00:01:16,853 --> 00:01:19,287
When it is finished, select Mark Resolved.

28
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:23,460
Back as the Tenant, the resolved ticket
shows a six-digit closure code.

29
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:26,938
The Tenant shares it only when the work is
done.

30
00:01:26,938 --> 00:01:29,372
The Company Admin enters the code under

31
00:01:29,372 --> 00:01:31,458
Close with OTP and selects Close.

32
00:01:31,458 --> 00:01:33,197
The ticket is now Closed.

33
00:01:33,197 --> 00:01:37,022
Its activity history records the
assignment, each status change and the

34
00:01:37,022 --> 00:01:40,500
closure with the code, with who did it and
when.

35
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:43,630
Ticket Reports counts tickets by status,
category and priority,

36
00:01:43,630 --> 00:01:46,759
with the average resolution time and the
average satisfaction.

37
00:01:46,759 --> 00:01:49,889
Finally, back as the Tenant, rate the
service: five

38
00:01:49,889 --> 00:01:52,671
stars and a short comment, then Submit
Rating.

39
00:01:52,671 --> 00:01:55,105
The rating is saved with the ticket

40
00:01:55,105 --> 00:01:57,192
and counts towards the satisfaction
average.
